From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsDmabuf <kmsdmabuf@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gem-cma: free imported objects through PRIME, not
 dma_free_attrs

drm_gem_cma_free_object() predates PRIME import in this tree: it always
calls drm_gem_cma_buf_destroy() -> dma_free_attrs(dev, size, vaddr, paddr).
That is only correct for objects drm_gem_cma_create() allocated.

An imported dma-buf is a drm_gem_cma_object wrapper owned by the importer:
vaddr is NULL (the exporter owns the pages), paddr is the exporter's
sg_dma_address and base.import_attach is set.  Freeing it through
dma_free_attrs() releases physical page 0 / the exporter's memory and leaks
the dma-buf attachment, dma-buf reference and mapped sg table.

Upstream fixed the same hole when it gained PRIME import (4.x
drm_gem_cma_free_object checks import_attach and calls
drm_prime_gem_destroy()).  Do the same here, taking the sg table from
driver_private -- the convention the importer uses because 3.10's
struct drm_gem_cma_object has no sgt field and the alternative would change
a shared header.

This is what makes .gem_free_object = drm_gem_cma_free_object safe for the
DECON KMS driver's mixed object set (imported scanout buffers from panfrost
and its own CMA dumb buffers, exynos_drm7580_main.c).

Fixes: KmsDmabuf / M2 dma-buf import.
Signed-off-by: KmsDmabuf <kmsdmabuf@local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem_cma_helper.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem_cma_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem_cma_helper.c
index 0a7e011..29dbe35 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem_cma_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gem_cma_helper.c
@@ -147,7 +147,21 @@ void drm_gem_cma_free_object(struct drm_gem_object *gem_obj)
 
 	cma_obj = to_drm_gem_cma_obj(gem_obj);
 
-	drm_gem_cma_buf_destroy(gem_obj->dev, cma_obj);
+	if (gem_obj->import_attach) {
+		/*
+		 * Imported dma-buf: the pages belong to the exporter, and
+		 * this wrapper owns nothing but the attachment.  The importer
+		 * stashed the sg table returned by dma_buf_map_attachment()
+		 * in driver_private; drm_prime_gem_destroy() unmaps it,
+		 * detaches the attachment and drops the dma-buf reference.
+		 * 3.10's struct drm_gem_cma_object has no sgt field, so the
+		 * pointer travels in the GEM object itself.
+		 */
+		drm_prime_gem_destroy(gem_obj, gem_obj->driver_private);
+		gem_obj->driver_private = NULL;
+	} else {
+		drm_gem_cma_buf_destroy(gem_obj->dev, cma_obj);
+	}
 
 	kfree(cma_obj);
 }
-- 
